  summary="Cities are promoting cycling for several reasons. Bicycles use road and parking space far more efficiently than cars, reducing congestion in crowded areas. Replacing car journeys with bike rides also lowers pollution and carbon emissions. Cycling improves people’s physical and mental health, which reduces demand on hospitals, and it is much cheaper for residents than owning a car, as well as quicker for short trips because cyclists avoid traffic and parking problems. Cities save money too, as cycle lanes are inexpensive to build and maintain. Finally, streets with fewer cars are quieter and more pleasant, and local businesses may gain because cyclists stop to shop more often.",
