   "Old buildings are more than bricks. They are a record of how people lived, worked and worshipped, and they give a town its identity. Walk through a historic quarter and you can read its past in the carved doorways and worn stone steps. Residents feel a sense of belonging to places that look like nowhere else, and many of these buildings hold shared memories: the school where grandparents studied, the hall where couples married.",
